{"id":"shimanami-kaido","title":"Shimanami Kaido","who":"Classic route · Japan's island-hopping bike path","when":"March–May and October–November","vehicle":"Any bike (rental), 1–2 days","kind":"bike","color":"#0284c7","summary":"About 70 km over the Seto Inland Sea on bridges linking six islands between Onomichi in Hiroshima and Imabari in Shikoku: a blue line painted on the road, citrus groves, temples, salt-making and a dedicated cycle lane on every bridge. Rent a bike at one end, drop it at the other.","sources":[{"label":"Cycling Mum Japan: Shimanami Kaido (October 2025)","url":"https://cyclingmumjapan.blogspot.com/2025/10/shimanami-kaido.html"},{"label":"i-tan: cycling islands, Shimanami Kaido (March 2025)","url":"https://i-tan.blogspot.com/2025/04/cycling-islands.html"}],"approximate":"The islands along the route.","km":88,"bbox":[132.9754,34.0656,133.2052,34.4087],"stops":[{"name":"Onomichi","place":"Onomichi, Japan","at":[34.4089,133.2052],"text":"A temple town on a hill; a 5-minute ferry to the first island.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Onomichi_Jodoji_05.JPG/500px-Onomichi_Jodoji_05.JPG","page":"Onomichi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Onomichi_Jodoji_05.JPG","credit":"by Reggaeman","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Mukaishima","place":"Mukaishima, Onomichi","at":[34.3828,133.1977],"text":"The first island.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Mukaishima_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Mukaishima_-_panoramio.jpg","page":"Mukaishima","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mukaishima_-_panoramio.jpg","credit":"z tanuki","license":"CC BY 3.0"}},{"name":"Innoshima","place":"Innoshima, Onomichi","at":[34.3451,133.1522],"text":"Over a bridge with a cycle deck under the road.","source":{"label":"i-tan (2025)","url":"https://i-tan.blogspot.com/2025/04/cycling-islands.html"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/INNOSHIMA_Island_2005.jpg/500px-INNOSHIMA_Island_2005.jpg","page":"Innoshima","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:INNOSHIMA_Island_2005.jpg","credit":"国土地理院","license":"Attribution"}},{"name":"Ikuchijima","place":"Ikuchijima","at":[34.3016,133.1472],"text":"Lemon groves and the extravagant Kōsan-ji temple.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/IKUCHI_-_SHIMA_Island_1947.jpg/500px-IKUCHI_-_SHIMA_Island_1947.jpg","page":"Ikuchijima","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IKUCHI_-_SHIMA_Island_1947.jpg","credit":"アメリカ軍","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Ōmishima","place":"Ōmishima","at":[34.2454,133.0229],"text":"The ancient Ōyamazumi shrine, full of samurai armour.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Ohyamazumi_Shrine_Haiden.JPG/500px-Ohyamazumi_Shrine_Haiden.JPG","page":"Ōyamazumi Shrine","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ohyamazumi_Shrine_Haiden.JPG","credit":"Mika-wa-Taro","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Hakatajima","place":"Hakatajima","at":[34.208,133.0763],"text":"Salt pans and quiet beaches.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Hakatajima_Island_from_Roadside_Station_%22Imabari_City_Tatara_Shimanami_Park%22_8.jpg/500px-Hakatajima_Island_from_Roadside_Station_%22Imabari_City_Tatara_Shimanami_Park%22_8.jpg","page":"Hakata Island","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hakatajima_Island_from_Roadside_Station_%22Imabari_City_Tatara_Shimanami_Park%22_8.jpg","credit":"そらみみ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Ōshima","place":"Ōshima, Imabari","at":[34.1921,133.0724],"text":"The fierce whirlpools of the Kurushima strait."},{"name":"Imabari","place":"Imabari, Japan","at":[34.0658,132.9977],"text":"Across the world's first triple suspension bridge to Shikoku.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Kurushimakaikyou_ohashi.jpg/500px-Kurushimakaikyou_ohashi.jpg","page":"Kurushima